Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:59:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 100/154] test(gestures): cover the coordinate flip the pinch
 hit test depends on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scoping the pinch to the sidebar already landed, and this adds what it was
missing. The AppKit to Views y flip sat unexported in an implementation file
with no direct coverage, and the browsertests around it only probe points near
the window's bottom edge, which is exactly where an off-by-a-height error hides.

It moves to a pure function tested at both edges.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 070442183a45d..46be246cead94 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -3542,6 +3542,8 @@ static_library("ui") {
       "atrium/atrium_peek_navigation_throttle.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_pinch_gesture_decision.h",
       "atrium/atrium_pinch_gesture_decision.cc",
+      "atrium/atrium_pinch_gesture_hit_test.h",
+      "atrium/atrium_pinch_gesture_hit_test.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_settings_window.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_hex_color.cc",
       "atrium/atrium_ambilight_cadence.cc",
